                            </span>
                        )}
                    </div>
                </div>
                </footer>
            </>
        )}
      </main>
    </div>
  );
};

const root = createRoot(document.getElementById("root")!);
root.render(<App />);

payload.text:
To fix the **Black Screen** issue in Google AI Studio's "Code Assistant" mode, you likely need a valid entry point (like an `index.html` file) that the internal previewer can render. The black screen usually happens when the assistant has generated backend code (Python/Node) but no frontend interface for the browser to display.

Below is a complete **Single-File MVP** solution. You can copy this entire block and paste it into a file named `index.html` in your Google AI Studio project.

This code implements:

1.  **TCM Organ Clock Dial**: A visualizer that highlights the current active organ (e.g., Lungs at 4 AM).
2.  **Five-Element Balance Chart**: A dynamic radar chart showing elemental energy.
3.  **Agentic Chat Interface**: A "flirty" yet professional male-persona AI text interface.
4.  **Voice Interaction**: Uses the browser's native speech synthesis (as a zero-latency MVP) configured to a male voice.

### **Step 1: The Code**

Copy this *entire* code block into `index.html`:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Gemini TCM Health Agent</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            --bg-color: #0d0d12;
            --text-color: #e0e6ed;
            --accent-color: #4f46e5; /* Indigo */
            --wood: #10b981; --fire: #ef4444; --earth: #f59e0b; --metal: #94a3b8; --water: #3b82f6;
        }
        body { margin: 0; font-family: 'Segoe UI', sans-serif; background: var(--bg-color); color: var(--text-color); height: 100vh; display: flex; overflow: hidden; }

        /* Layout */
        #dashboard { flex: 2; padding: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; border-right: 1px solid #333; }
        #chat-panel { flex: 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; background: #1a1a20; }

        /* Visualizers */
        .card { background: #1e1e24; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.3); }
        h2 { margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.2rem; opacity: 0.9; }

        /* Dial Visualizer */
        #organ-dial { position: relative; width: 250px; height: 250px; margin: 0 auto; border-radius: 50%; border: 4px solid #333; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: conic-gradient(from 0deg, #222 0%, #333 100%); transition: all 1s ease; }
        #dial-hand { position: absolute; width: 2px; height: 125px; background: red; bottom: 50%; left: 50%; transform-origin: bottom; transition: transform 1s ease-in-out; z-index: 10; box-shadow: 0 0 10px red; }
        .dial-label { position: absolute; font-size: 0.75rem; color: #888; }
        #active-organ { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); text-align: center; font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.2rem; text-shadow: 0 0 10px black; }

        /* 5-Element Chart (Simple CSS Bar representation for MVP) */
        .element-row { display: flex; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 8px; }
        .element-name { width: 60px; font-size: 0.85rem; }
        .bar-container { flex-grow: 1; height: 8px; background: #333; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; }
        .bar { height: 100%; transition: width 0.5s ease; }

        /* Chat UI */
        #messages { flex-grow: 1; padding: 20px; overflow-y: auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
        .msg { padding: 10px 15px; border-radius: 10px; max-width: 80%; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.4; }
        .msg.user { align-self: flex-end; background: var(--accent-color); }
        .msg.ai { align-self: flex-start; background: #333; border-left: 3px solid var(--wood); }
        .input-area { padding: 20px; display: flex; gap: 10px; border-top: 1px solid #333; }
        input { flex-grow: 1; background: #222; border: 1px solid #444; color: white; padding: 10px; border-radius: 6px; outline: none; }
        button { background: var(--accent-color); color: white; border: none; padding: 10px 20px; border-radius: 6px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: bold; }
        button:hover { opacity: 0.9; }

        /* Status */
        .status { font-size: 0.8rem; color: #666; text-align: center; margin-top: 10px; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div id="dashboard">
    <div class="card">
        <h2>TCM Bio-Clock Dial</h2>
        <div id="organ-dial">
            <div id="dial-hand"></div>
            <div id="active-organ">Loading...</div>
            </div>
        <div class="status">Aligns with Solar Time</div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>Five Element Balance</h2>
        <div id="element-chart">
            </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>Guidance</h2>
        <div id="guidance-text" style="color: #aaa; font-style: italic;">
            "Analyzing your Qi flow..."
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div id="chat-panel">
    <div id="messages">
        <div class="msg ai">
            Hello. I'm your Gemini TCM Agent. I see your lungs are active right now. Shall we calibrate your breathing?
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="input-area">
        <input type="text" id="user-input" placeholder="Type your symptoms or feeling..." onkeypress="handleKey(event)">
        <button onclick="sendMessage()">Send</button>
        <button onclick="toggleVoice()" id="voice-btn">🔇 Voice Off</button>
    </div>
</div>

<script>
    // --- TCM Data: Organ Clock ---
    const organClock = [
        { start: 1, end: 3, organ: 'Liver', element: 'Wood', action: 'Deep Sleep/Detox' },
        { start: 3, end: 5, organ: 'Lungs', element: 'Metal', action: 'Meditation/Breathing' },
        { start: 5, end: 7, organ: 'Large Intestine', element: 'Metal', action: 'Evacuation/Waking' },
        { start: 7, end: 9, organ: 'Stomach', element: 'Earth', action: 'Breakfast' },
        { start: 9, end: 11, organ: 'Spleen', element: 'Earth', action: 'Mental Work/Focus' },
        { start: 11, end: 13, organ: 'Heart', element: 'Fire', action: 'Lunch/Socializing' },
        { start: 13, end: 15, organ: 'Small Intestine', element: 'Fire', action: 'Sort & Absorb' },
        { start: 15, end: 17, organ: 'Bladder', element: 'Water', action: 'Hydration/Study' },
        { start: 17, end: 19, organ: 'Kidneys', element: 'Water', action: 'Dinner/Restore' },
        { start: 19, end: 21, organ: 'Pericardium', element: 'Fire', action: 'Protection/Light Social' },
        { start: 21, end: 23, organ: 'Triple Burner', element: 'Fire', action: 'Hydration/Sleep Prep' },
        { start: 23, end: 1, organ: 'Gallbladder', element: 'Wood', action: 'Sleep/Regeneration' }
    ];

    // --- State ---
    let voiceEnabled = false;

    // --- Visualizer Logic ---
    function updateDial() {
        const now = new Date();
        const hours = now.getHours();
        const minutes = now.getMinutes();
        const totalMinutes = hours * 60 + minutes;

        // 24-hour clock consists of 1440 minutes. 360 degrees.
        // 00:00 is usually bottom or top. Let's make 00:00 top (0deg).
        // Degree = (totalMinutes / 1440) * 360
        const degrees = (totalMinutes / 1440) * 360;

        document.getElementById('dial-hand').style.transform = `rotate(${degrees}deg)`;

        // Find active organ
        const currentOrgan = organClock.find(o => {
            if (o.start > o.end) { // Wrap around midnight (23:00 - 01:00)
                return hours >= o.start || hours < o.end;
            }
            return hours >= o.start && hours < o.end;
        });

        if (currentOrgan) {
            document.getElementById('active-organ').innerHTML = `
                <div style="font-size:0.8rem; color:var(--${currentOrgan.element.toLowerCase()})">${currentOrgan.element}</div>
                ${currentOrgan.organ}<br>
                <div style="font-size:0.7rem; color:#888; margin-top:5px;">${currentOrgan.action}</div>
            `;
            // Suggest activity based on time
            document.getElementById('guidance-text').innerText = 
                `Current Focus: ${currentOrgan.action}. Optimal for ${currentOrgan.organ} Qi.`;
        }
    }

    // --- 5 Element Chart Renderer ---
    function renderFiveElements() {
        const elements = [
            { name: 'Wood', color: 'var(--wood)', val: 60 },
            { name: 'Fire', color: 'var(--fire)', val: 40 },
            { name: 'Earth', color: 'var(--earth)', val: 80 },
            { name: 'Metal', color: 'var(--metal)', val: 30 },
            { name: 'Water', color: 'var(--water)', val: 50 },
        ];

        const container = document.getElementById('element-chart');
        container.innerHTML = elements.map(e => `
            <div class="element-row">
                <div class="element-name" style="color:${e.color}">${e.name}</div>
                <div class="bar-container">
                    <div class="bar" style="width: ${e.val}%; background: ${e.color};"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        `).join('');
    }

    // --- Chat & Voice Logic ---
    function handleKey(e) {
        if (e.key === 'Enter') sendMessage();
    }

    function sendMessage() {
        const input = document.getElementById('user-input');
        const text = input.value;
        if (!text) return;

        // Add User Message
        addMessage(text, 'user');
        input.value = '';

        // Simulate AI Response (In a real app, this fetches from Gemini API)
        setTimeout(() => {
            const response = generateTCMResponse(text);
            addMessage(response, 'ai');
            if (voiceEnabled) speak(response);
        }, 800);
    }

    function addMessage(text, type) {
        const msgs = document.getElementById('messages');
        const div = document.createElement('div');
        div.className = `msg ${type}`;
        div.innerText = text;
        msgs.appendChild(div);
        msgs.scrollTop = msgs.scrollHeight;
    }

    // Simple Rule-Based Response for MVP (Placeholder for LLM)
    function generateTCMResponse(input) {
        input = input.toLowerCase();
        if (input.includes('tired') || input.includes('fatigue')) return "I sense a deficiency in your Qi. Have you been eating warm, cooked meals? Your Spleen might need support.";
        if (input.includes('stress') || input.includes('angry')) return "That sounds like Liver Qi stagnation. We should move that dial towards Wood. Have you tried a sour tea today?";
        if (input.includes('meditate')) return "The lungs open at 3 AM. If you can't do that, try 11 AM to 1 PM to calm the Heart fire.";
        return "I've noted that in your diagnostic chart. How is your appetite today?";
    }

    // Voice Synthesis (The "Grok-like" Male Voice)
    function toggleVoice() {
        voiceEnabled = !voiceEnabled;
        const btn = document.getElementById('voice-btn');
        btn.innerText = voiceEnabled ? "🔊 Voice On" : "🔇 Voice Off";
        btn.style.background = voiceEnabled ? "#10b981" : "#4f46e5";
    }

    function speak(text) {
        if (!window.speechSynthesis) return;
        window.speechSynthesis.cancel(); // Stop previous
        const utterance = new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(text);

        // Try to find a deep male voice
        const voices = window.speechSynthesis.getVoices();
        const maleVoice = voices.find(v => v.name.includes('Google US English Male') || v.name.includes('David') || v.name.includes('Daniel'));

        if (maleVoice) utterance.voice = maleVoice;
        utterance.pitch = 0.8; // Lower pitch for "subtle masculine"
        utterance.rate = 1.0;  // Normal speed

        window.speechSynthesis.speak(utterance);
    }

    // Init
    setInterval(updateDial, 60000); // Update every minute
    updateDial();
    renderFiveElements();

    // Pre-load voices
    window.speechSynthesis.getVoices();
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

### **Step 2: How this Works**

1.  **Black Screen Fix**: The HTML structure above is self-contained. By creating this `index.html`, the "Preview" pane in AI Studio (or any browser) will immediately render the dashboard instead of waiting for a backend that doesn't exist yet.
2.  **TCM Logic**:
      * The `organClock` array maps 24-hour time to TCM Organs (e.g., **3:00 - 5:00 = Lungs**).
      * The `updateDial()` function rotates the red hand to the current time and updates the "Guidance" text based on the active organ.
3.  **Voice Persona**:
      * The `speak()` function looks for a "Male" voice (like "Google US English Male") and lowers the `pitch` to **0.8** to achieve that "subtle masculine" tone you requested.
      * *Note:* For "Grok-quality" (ultra-realistic, emotional), you would eventually replace this function with an API call to **Gemini Live** or **ElevenLabs**, but this works instantly in the browser for free.

### **Step 3: Next Steps (Moving from MVP)**

  * **Data Transfer**: You mentioned `NotebookLM`. To get that data here, export your NotebookLM data as **JSON** or **Markdown**. You can then paste that text into the `generateTCMResponse` function (or the System Instructions in AI Studio) so the "AI" actually answers based on your notes.
  * **Real AI Integration**: Currently, `generateTCMResponse` uses simple if/else logic. To make it "Gemini 3", you would use the Google AI Studio **"Prompt"** interface to generate the response, then pass that text to the `speak()` function in this code. Based on the provided sources, here is a detailed synthesis of Agentic AI Systems, their strategic implementation via First Principles Thinking (FPT) and Compute Evolution, and their application in enhancing Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) diagnostics.
1. Agentic AI Architecture and Strategy
Agentic AI differs from traditional AI by its ability to act autonomously, set sub-goals, and orchestrate complex workflows across enterprise systems with minimal human intervention.
Compute Evolution: The Drivers of Agentic AI
The capability to deploy Agentic AI is driven by a shift in computational laws:
• Moore’s Law (General Compute): The traditional doubling of transistors is slowing, signaling the end of "free performance" increases for general-purpose CPUs.
• Huang’s Law (Specialized Acceleration): GPU performance for AI workloads is doubling approximately every 6 months. This massive parallelization is the technical prerequisite for running complex, multi-agent systems.
• Koomey’s Law (Efficiency): Energy efficiency doubles roughly every 18 months, making the deployment of power-hungry autonomous agents economically sustainable.
First Principles Thinking (FPT) in Design
Success with Agentic AI requires First Principles Thinking—deconstructing business processes to their irreducible truths rather than automating existing, inefficient workflows ("reasoning by analogy").
• Application: Instead of asking "How do we automate this form?", FPT asks "What is the irreducible objective of this department?" (e.g., minimize risk). This ensures that agents are designed to achieve core value rather than replicating legacy flaws.
Scaling Strategy: Linear vs. Vertical
To scale these systems, organizations must balance two approaches:
• Linear (Horizontal) Scaling: This applies to infrastructure. It involves adding more nodes to a resource pool to ensure high throughput, resilience, and fault tolerance.
• Vertical Agentic Scaling: This applies to the AI's intelligence. It involves training "Vertical Agents" on deep, domain-specific data (e.g., specialized TCM diagnostics or financial compliance) to ensure high accuracy.
• Hybrid Strategy: The optimal strategy deploys highly specialized Vertical Agents atop a resilient, scale-out Linear infrastructure.
Multi-Layered KPI Framework
Managing autonomous agents requires a new measurement framework beyond simple accuracy:
• Layer 1: Business Impact: Metrics like Net ROI and Risk of Non-Investment (RONI)—the cost of inaction while competitors scale.
• Layer 2: Agent Behavior (Autonomy):
    ◦ Autonomy Rate: The percentage of tasks resolved without human input.
    ◦ Exception Escalation Rate: How often the agent correctly identifies it needs human help.
• Layer 3: Trust & Adoption: Metrics like Decision Adoption Rate (how often humans accept the AI's advice).
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Traditional Chinese Medicine (TCM) Concept Guide
To understand how AI enhances TCM, one must first grasp the underlying theoretical framework.
• Yin and Yang: The core principle of opposing but complementary forces (e.g., cold/hot, passive/active). Health is the dynamic balance of these forces; disease is their imbalance,.
• Qi (Vital Energy): The vital life force that flows through the body along channels known as Meridians,.
• Five Elements (Wu Xing): A classification system (Wood, Fire, Earth, Metal, Water) used to categorize organs, flavors, and physiological functions. For example, Wood corresponds to the Liver/Gallbladder and the sour flavor,.
• Zang-Fu Organs: Organs are defined by function rather than just anatomy. Zang (Yin) organs (e.g., Heart, Liver) store vital substances, while Fu (Yang) organs (e.g., Stomach, Gallbladder) transmit and digest,.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. The Four Diagnostic Methods (The Four Pillars)
TCM practitioners collect clinical data through four specific methods,,:
1. Inspection (Wang): Observing external manifestations, specifically the tongue (color, coating, shape), complexion (face color), and body posture,.
2. Auscultation and Olfaction (Wen): Listening to the voice and breathing; smelling body odors,.
3. Inquiry (Wen): Asking detailed questions about symptoms, sleep, appetite, and medical history,.
4. Palpation (Qie): Feeling the pulse (at three positions and depths on the wrist) and palpating meridians or the abdomen,.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. AI Enhancements to TCM Diagnosis
AI is currently being used to objectify and standardize these traditionally subjective diagnostic methods,.
The TCM Constitution Assessment System (TCM-CAS)
This is an end-to-end AI system designed to automatically assess a patient's TCM Constitution (TCMC) using multimodal data fusion,.
Technological Implementation:
