    1. Image Modality (Face & Tongue): Uses Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) and encoders like SigLIP to extract features such as facial color, lip color, tongue coating, and texture,.
    2. Text Modality (Inquiry): Uses Graph Neural Networks (GraphSAGE) to process questionnaire responses about symptoms (e.g., fatigue),.
    3. Pulse Diagnosis: Uses deep learning models (e.g., ResNet, LeNet) to analyze pulse waveforms for detecting conditions like diabetes,.
Integration Architecture (RAG & MCP): To ensure these AI agents are accurate and grounded in medical reality, the system utilizes:
• RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation): A "Knowledge Agent" retrieves authoritative TCM texts to ground the AI's recommendations, ensuring they are based on established theory rather than hallucination,.
• MCP (Model Context Protocol): A "Data Agent" uses the MCP Toolbox to securely query structured SQL databases containing user health metrics and TCM biomarkers,.
Output: The AI synthesizes this data to provide an "Organ Vitality Score" and personalized dietary recommendations (e.g., specific foods to balance a "Damp-Heat" constitution), bridging ancient wisdom with data-driven precision,.

